Original commit body from 4ad53ce48c9402df56e76b48683e5a1fec660ce3:

solidity.py emitted kind="function" for every function definition,
whether declared inside a contract/interface/library body or at file
scope. Every other OO analyzer distinguishes the two, and consumers key
on it -- most visibly link_type_hierarchy, which indexes dispatch
candidates with `if sym.kind != "method": continue`.

Measured on openzeppelin-contracts: 2,025 members of type-like
containers, 100% kind=function, zero kind=method -- the only 100% cell in
the corpus (ruby 814/0, kotlin 1140/0, java 1040/0 the other way). 516
inherits edges over 164 parents, and not one parent had a single
method-kind member, so the parent-method lookup returned empty for every
one of them.

Containment now decides the kind, as everywhere else: a function with an
enclosing contract/interface/library is a method; a file-scope free
function (legal since Solidity 0.7) stays a function. constructor,
modifier and event keep their own kinds -- distinct constructs, not
functions with a receiver.

RESULT, with INV-nosoz: openzeppelin-contracts goes 0 -> 877 solidity
dispatches_to. Neither fix produces that alone -- INV-nosoz got the edge
to the dispatch map and moved the repo by ZERO; this supplies the members
it found waiting there. That is why they were filed and measured
separately. test_interface_dispatch_parity's solidity cell, a STRICT
xfail, now XPASSes and is retired -- the second cell that gate has given
up this cycle.

I NEARLY SHIPPED A REGRESSION AND ONLY THE CORPUS CAUGHT IT. The first
cut fixed the four `kind == "function"` literals inside solidity.py (the
span index, the `using X for Y` resolver, both halves of the overrides
walker) and passed every test, including five edge-survival controls
written specifically to catch a missed reader. The corpus then showed
calls down 6,689 (-43%) and 1,249 nodes gone: a FIFTH and SIXTH copy in
hypergumbo_core.linkers.solidity_abi, a different package, filtering on
("function", "constructor"). It silently stopped minting ABI call-site
nodes -- the JS<->Solidity boundary -- and nothing raised. A count just
dropped. Both packages now read one SOLIDITY_CALLABLE_DECLARATION_KINDS
in core, pinned from the producer side, since a constant duplicated
across a package boundary drifts into a terminal rather than into CI.

Re-measured after the repair, the delta is clean: nodes 13332 -> 13332,
and dispatches_to is the ONLY edge type that changed.

IDENTITY: kind is a slot in both Symbol.id and the typed stable_id, so
contract-member ids CHANGE. A producer correction, not a scheme change --
the formula is untouched, the input is now right -- but the values are
not comparable across the boundary. Disclosed in CHANGELOG.

The G1 runtime_coherence ratchet correctly breached: (method/solidity ->
method/solidity) began carrying dispatches_to alongside overrides. The
partition became visible because the fix WORKED, not because anything
degraded -- before, it carried only overrides. Allow-listed as legitimate
(overrides runs child->parent, dispatches_to parent->child: opposite
directions, one endpoint shape), exactly as WI-duguk's rust trait
partition was. The baseline stays 1; it was not raised.

The 30 analyzer tests that broke were selectors, not kind assertions.
They are now kind-agnostic; test_solidity_member_kind.py owns the kind
contract alone, so a future kind change breaks exactly one file on
purpose. test_callable_kinds_carry_stable_id gained a file-scope function
so both arms are covered -- its old fixture would have gone silently
vacuous.

10,877 passed; mypy ratchet clean.

